  "id": "OSEC-2026-25",
  "modified": "2026-10-28T09:15:50Z",
  "published": "2026-10-23T21:30:00Z",
  "summary": "Heap buffer overflow in the OCaml `runtime_events` consumer when parsing an oversized custom user event",
  "details": "ANT-2026-0JXJVEVY\n\nCustom events maintains a cache of user events, it is possible to have a corrupt stream that has a valid message with one message type (which can be custom/unit/span/int) and then has the same event with a different message type.\n\nThis would never be encountered in a real program but can lead to a crash.\n\n## Fix\n\nCheck message lengths for all runtime event types, report a corrupt stream on mismatch.\n\n## Am I affected?\n\nIf the runtime events producer and consumer run in separate processes, and the producer can be tricked into producing malformed data.\n\n## Timeline\n\n- 2026-08-24: vulnerability was found\n- 2026-08-27: forwarded report to security@ocaml.org\n- 2027-09-05: fix merged to trunk",
